Z||000031||WKDFIRO||12-22-2001||02:50 AM||||Now there is the Archie I know and mock!<P>I still say that I am glad that not all Fiero owners in Illinois are of the caliber of Archie. I would say to everyone not to consider Archie a typical Fiero person. And no matter however the hell he spells his name or anyone spells his name, I can't help but think it should just be spelled Ass first, then Hole last. <P>I do apologize, ejay, that Ass (for short)couldn't seem to control himself by interjecting some Illinois hick humor into an otherwise straight forward thread. Apparently he feels that he needs to prove something. Though Eric has actually picked up some social grace in handling Mr. Hole, Mr. Hole has proven that he can't be much more than belligerent  with small sparks of insight. <P>"Everytime you take me on..."<P>What a joke you are. <P>There was nothing here to do with you, nothing here that should have aggravated you and truely nothing here to concern you. But you have to come in and show why some have not liked you for much longer than some have not liked George Miller. <P>Im not here to save anyone's butt. Im just here to say you are in the wrong. You were not provoked and you had no reason to carry on like you did. <P>So why don't you find a Fiero under some tree and go butcher it. <P>There might be a reason why in the car capital of the world, Southern California, with more hot rods and custom rides on the road in December than all the custom jobs in certain east coast states put together that there aren't more V8 Fieros from Mr. Hole. One would think that every other Fiero would have a V8 in Southern California. But it would almost seem that we would rather NOT have a V8 than deal with Mr. Hole. Fiero Motorsports wouldn't touch V8 kits from you. And your former customers did beg quite a bit. I often wondered whatever became of their Fieros after that.<P>I might be wrong. The kit cars maybe snatching the V8s up left and right. But most of those Fieros are being butchered up to become something else, so I can see how one might not notice. But as they say, there is always someone to build a better electric water pump.<P>Im not taking you on, Mr. Hole. You are just too annoying to be worth anymore of my time. <P>I apologize to Cliff, this Forum and the Fiero Clubs of Illinois for this breach of ettiquette, but I just couldn't let this one go by.<P>And I apologize once again to ejayerik for this outburst. I guess we California beach bums don't stand kindly to some hick back east talking trash no matter how funny he might think he is.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||9
